WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.500 line:0
Hold’em: use two hole cards and five board
cards to make the best five-card hand.

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:06.999 line:0
North holds A♠A♥ on the button;
East posts the 10 blind, South the 20.

00:00:06.999 --> 00:00:14.999 line:0
Preflop, North acts first and clicks
Call 20 to match the big blind.

00:00:14.999 --> 00:00:19.899 line:0
Fast-forward: East calls, South checks;
the flop is dealt.

00:00:19.899 --> 00:00:23.999 line:0
Flop A♣ 9♦ 5♠ gives North three aces.
East and South check.

00:00:23.999 --> 00:00:31.999 line:0
North clicks Bet, enters 100 and confirms.
The amount is the street’s total bet.

00:00:31.999 --> 00:00:36.599 line:0
Fast-forward: East folds, South calls 100.
A fold forfeits the chips already in the pot.

00:00:36.599 --> 00:00:40.999 line:0
The turn J♥ and river 2♣ follow;
street bets reset and both players check.

00:00:40.999 --> 00:00:45.299 line:0
On the river North clicks Check.

00:00:45.299 --> 00:00:51.998 line:0
Showdown: North’s three aces win the pot.
The next hand starts, button on East.

00:00:51.998 --> 00:00:58.248 line:0
Fast-forward: hand two. East calls 20,
South goes all-in for 880.

00:00:58.248 --> 00:01:00.997 line:0
North calls 880; East goes all-in to 980,
only 100 more: not a full raise.

00:01:00.997 --> 00:01:05.297 line:0
North clicks Call 100 to match 980.

00:01:05.297 --> 00:01:11.997 line:0
Main pot 2,640: all three. Side pot 200: only
North and East. North’s aces win both.

00:01:11.997 --> 00:01:21.000 line:0
North wins every chip, 3,000, and the match ends.
Otherwise 20 hands are played and chips decide.
